      answerHtml: `<p>Supply, mostly. Single-family homes in Lutz closed at a median <strong>24 days on market</strong> for the twelve months ending October 2026, against 27 days in Tampa and 39 in Riverview, and Lutz is not absorbing large volumes of new master-planned construction the way Riverview and Wesley Chapel are.</p><p>Add a well-regarded high school zone and a straightforward run down the Veterans Expressway or Dale Mabry Highway into Tampa, and demand consistently outruns the number of homes listed. The flip side shows up in the condo numbers: Lutz condos took about <strong>75 days</strong> at a $205,000 median, because that segment is small and the buyer pool for it here is thin. If you are selling, start with a <a href="/free-home-valuation/" class="text-link hover:underline">free home valuation</a>.</p>`,
