      answerHtml: `<p>They are two separate governments and you pay both. The <strong>Westchase Community Development District</strong> is a Chapter 190 special-purpose unit of local government created by Hillsborough County ordinance; it built and maintains the community-wide infrastructure, and owners repay those bonds through an annual debt service assessment plus an operations and maintenance assessment. It runs a field office at 9515 W Linebaugh Avenue.</p><p>Separately, the <strong>Westchase Community Association</strong> is the HOA handling covenants and community standards, and many individual villages inside Westchase have their own sub-association on top of that. Before you make an offer, get the CDD assessment, the WCA dues, and the village-level dues for that exact address in writing.</p>`,
