      answerHtml: `<p>Westchase is not one subdivision, it is a collection of villages inside a single master plan, and the village determines your sub-association dues and often your product type.</p><p><strong>West Park Village</strong> is the one people picture: a walkable village center with townhomes, smaller-lot homes, shops, and restaurants, and the closest thing to a downtown that 33626 has. <strong>The Bridges</strong>, <strong>Stonebridge</strong>, <strong>Harbor Links</strong>, and <strong>Glencliff</strong> cover the rest of the range, from golf-adjacent to conventional single-family. Because each village has its own covenants, fee schedule, and architectural rules, two homes at the same price in Westchase can carry very different monthly obligations. Always ask which village. Browse <a href="/westchase-homes-for-sale/" class="text-link hover:underline">Westchase homes for sale</a>.</p>`,
