      answerHtml: `<p>Price, speed, and water. For the twelve months ending October 2026, single-family homes in ZIP 33626 (Westchase) closed at about a <strong>$700,000 median in 15 days</strong>, while the 33615/33634/33635 ZIPs that make up <a href="/town-n-country/" class="text-link hover:underline">Town 'n' Country</a> closed at about <strong>$450,000 in 27 days</strong>.</p><p>Westchase is a single planned community with a CDD, an HOA, and village sub-associations; Town 'n' Country is a large unincorporated area of mostly 1960s-through-1990s subdivisions, much of it without a CDD at all. The other real difference is surge exposure, parts of Town 'n' Country sit in low-lying ground near Rocky Creek and Sweetwater Creek, and the county recently moved some of those neighborhoods into Evacuation Zone A.</p>`,
