      answerHtml: `<p>No, Temple Terrace is its own incorporated city, one of only three in Hillsborough County alongside <a href="/tampa/" class="text-link hover:underline">Tampa</a> and <a href="/plant-city/" class="text-link hover:underline">Plant City</a>. It was incorporated by legislative act in <strong>May 1925</strong>, at the peak of the Florida land boom, and it has its own city council, police department, and millage rate.</p><p>It is surrounded by Tampa and unincorporated Hillsborough on all sides, and it shares ZIP codes <strong>33617 and 33637</strong> with adjacent unincorporated areas, which is exactly why buyers get confused. A 33617 address is not automatically inside the city limits. Since city limits determine your tax bill and your municipal services, verify the jurisdiction for the specific parcel.</p>`,
